  "query_preview": "/SATURDAY THROUGH TUESDAY/... \nThe upcoming weekend calls for the Pacific ridge to remain \ndominant across our region, but it will be in a weakening phase \nand is likely to get knocked down by a fast moving disturbance \npassing across the Four Corners area. Even with H5 heights \ndropping to between 580-583dm, temperatures are not expected to \ndrop much with lower desert highs at least maintaining mid 70s for\nhighs. The weather pattern suggests another brief shortwave ridge\nmoving through on Monday and/or Tuesday, but models are favoring \na gradual increase in moisture early next week pushing PWAT \nanomalies to around 150-175% of normal by Tuesday. Temperatures \nare not expected to change much early next week despite the \nexpected increase in clouds. Models then favor a more significant\nPacific disturbance approaching the California coast and then \nlikely passing through our region during the middle of next week. \nThe timing, strength, and exact track of the system is still quite\nuncertain, but there are at least decent signs it will contain \nadequate moisture for some precipitation chances for our region. \nWe expect it will be at least a few more days until we have a good\nidea on rain potential for next week's weather system.",
